<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady; oil, meal up.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady; oil, meal up.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in dull trade in central India on Friday, traders said.</p>
<p>They said soybean, offered for plant delivery, however, gained 50-100 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Business volumes were low because of poor arrivals,</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was up 100 rupees per tonne because of reduced supplies. Soyoil refined was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were slightly up due to poor supply. Soymeal yellow was quoted at $108-$109 per tonne. Rapeseed extraction was offered at 3,850 rupees for ready delivery and at 3,700 rupees for March delivery (f.o.r).</p>
